# Nucleon momentum distribution n(k) for the deuteron, AV18.
#
# Source: R. B. Wiringa, Argonne National Laboratory,
#   https://www.phy.anl.gov/theory/research/momenta/  ->  h2.momentum
#   (2H(1+), AV18; cite Wiringa et al., Phys. Rev. C 89, 024305 (2014)).
#   Raw file kept in data/source/h2_av18_rhok.txt.
#
# n(k) = RHOK(k) / (2 pi)^3, which reproduces the D2 column of Figure 47 of the
# RGC note to 4e-4 over its range k = 0 .. 1.9 fm^-1 -- the figure is this table,
# truncated.  (At k = 0 the ANL file prints RHOK to 4 digits, giving 12.957
# against the note's 13.021; k = 0 carries zero weight in 4 pi k^2 n(k).)
#
# Range: the figure stops at 1.9 fm^-1, which holds only 97.6% of the norm but
# leaves out 44% of <k^2>.  This file runs to 7.4 fm^-1, beyond which the VMC
# result sits on its statistical noise floor and turns unphysical.  Use the
# sampler's k_max option to cut it shorter.
#
#   Int 4 pi k^2 n(k) dk = 0.999976   over 0 .. 7.4 fm^-1
#   <|p|> = 95.6 MeV/c,  p_rms = 136.3 MeV/c
#
# Column 1: k   [fm^-1]
# Column 2: n(k) [fm^3]
#
#      k            n(k)
